    "heading": "Duration",
    "lineStart": 7223,
    "lineEnd": 7231
  },
  "section": "7.22",
  "rulesText": "A spell's duration is the length of time the spell persists after it is cast. A duration typically takes one of the following forms:\n\nConcentration. A duration that requires Concentration follows the Concentration rules (see “Rules Glossary”).\n\nInstantaneous. An instantaneous duration means the spell's magic appears only for a moment and then disappears.\n\nTime Span. A duration that provides a time span specifies how long the spell lasts in rounds, minutes, hours, or the like. For example, a Duration entry might say “1 minute,” meaning the spell ends after 1 minute has passed. While a time-span spell that you cast is ongoing, you can dismiss it (no action required) if you don’t have the Incapacitated condition.",
  "mentionsCondition": [
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/objects/conditions/incapacitated"
    }
  ]
}
